1. Uses `sqlite::connect()` to connect to "test_db.sqlite"
2. Uses `read<std::vector<Event>>` to specify we want to read Event records into a vector
3. Pipes to `order_by("created_at"_c.desc())` to order by created_at in descending order (most recent first)
4. Pipes to `limit(n)` to restrict results to N events
5. Executes the query with `result(conn)` and extracts the value with `.value()`

